\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The same geometry as Fig.~\ref {fig:rve-dimensions}, now meshed with standard displacement-based finite elements. The outer boundary (red) carries the prescribed affine macro-strain Dirichlet condition; the remaining boundary and interior nodes, including the hole boundary, are free. The cell geometry has $D_4$ (square) symmetry, but the PANN construction in this paper does not assume or exploit it; see Section~\ref {sec:related-klein-linden}.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rve-geometry}{{2}{5}{The same geometry as Fig.~\ref {fig:rve-dimensions}, now meshed with standard displacement-based finite elements. The outer boundary (red) carries the prescribed affine macro-strain Dirichlet condition; the remaining boundary and interior nodes, including the hole boundary, are free. The cell geometry has $D_4$ (square) symmetry, but the PANN construction in this paper does not assume or exploit it; see Section~\ref {sec:related-klein-linden}}{figure.2}{}}
