\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The four closed strain loops evaluated in Table~\ref {tab:cyclic}: a genuine 3D view (left) and the three pairwise projections (right), so every loop's shape is visible from some panel without ambiguity. The small square and the shear loop each vary only two of the three strain components (they collapse to a flat segment in whichever projection does not involve their varying components); the origin-anchored ellipse and the mixed triangle both move in all three simultaneously, and only the ellipse starts and returns to the true reference state $\bm  {\varepsilon }=\bm  {0}$ (the black marker).}}{9}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cyclic-loops}{{6}{9}{The four closed strain loops evaluated in Table~\ref {tab:cyclic}: a genuine 3D view (left) and the three pairwise projections (right), so every loop's shape is visible from some panel without ambiguity. The small square and the shear loop each vary only two of the three strain components (they collapse to a flat segment in whichever projection does not involve their varying components); the origin-anchored ellipse and the mixed triangle both move in all three simultaneously, and only the ellipse starts and returns to the true reference state $\bm \varepsilon =\bm 0$ (the black marker)}{figure.6}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Cyclic work $\DOTSI \ointop \ilimits@ _{\mathcal  L}\bm  {S}\cdot d\bm  {\varepsilon }$ (Pa) around four closed strain loops, trapezoidal quadrature, $12800{}$ points per edge. Exactly zero is expected, by \eqref  {eq:cyclic}, for tiers 2--3b; nothing constrains tier 1. Convergence of this resolution is verified in Figure~\ref {fig:cyclic-convergence}.}}{10}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:cyclic}{{2}{10}{Cyclic work $\oint _{\mathcal L}\bm S\cdot d\bm \varepsilon $ (Pa) around four closed strain loops, trapezoidal quadrature, $\CyclicPointsPerEdge {}$ points per edge. Exactly zero is expected, by \eqref {eq:cyclic}, for tiers 2--3b; nothing constrains tier 1. Convergence of this resolution is verified in Figure~\ref {fig:cyclic-convergence}}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Residual magnitude on the mixed-triangle loop vs.\ quadrature points per edge, log-log, at the four refinement levels $200, 800, 3200, 12800{}$. The three energy-based tiers fall on the slope expected of $\mathcal  O(h^2)$ trapezoidal quadrature error (dotted reference line) and are converging to the true value of exactly zero; the tier-1 residual does not move. The free-hyperelastic tier's residual (tier 2, evaluated in float32) levels off around $10^{-1}$--$1\,\mathrm  {Pa}$ at the finest level rather than continuing to shrink, consistent with floating-point precision rather than remaining quadrature error; the two float64 tiers (3a/3b) keep converging cleanly throughout.}}{10}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cyclic-convergence}{{7}{10}{Residual magnitude on the mixed-triangle loop vs.\ quadrature points per edge, log-log, at the four refinement levels $\CyclicRefinementLevels {}$. The three energy-based tiers fall on the slope expected of $\mathcal O(h^2)$ trapezoidal quadrature error (dotted reference line) and are converging to the true value of exactly zero; the tier-1 residual does not move. The free-hyperelastic tier's residual (tier 2, evaluated in float32) levels off around $10^{-1}$--$1\,\mathrm {Pa}$ at the finest level rather than continuing to shrink, consistent with floating-point precision rather than remaining quadrature error; the two float64 tiers (3a/3b) keep converging cleanly throughout}{figure.7}{}}
