\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The volumetric barrier $h(J)$ in isolation, with no feature or network terms and no coupling to a stretching path, for the trained coefficients $r=2.0390e-01$, $\beta =2.2357e-09$. Left: near $J=1$, $h(J)$ and $-r\log J$ alone are visually indistinguishable, and both diverge as $J\to 0^+$. Right: on a log scale, $-r\log J$ alone decreases without bound, and $h(J)$ tracks it closely until the quadratic term alone finally overtakes it near $J^\ast \approx 9550$, the point where $h(J)$ starts to grow. This $J^\ast $ is far beyond any dilation this RVE's data ever reaches; the total trained energy nonetheless grows steeply for realistic stretches, driven by the sixth-power terms of Proposition~\ref {prop:sixth-power-bound} below rather than by $h(J)$ itself (Figure~\ref {fig:volumetric}).}}{19}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:volumetric-isolated}{{9}{19}{The volumetric barrier $h(J)$ in isolation, with no feature or network terms and no coupling to a stretching path, for the trained coefficients $r=\BarrierCoefficient $, $\beta =\QuadraticCoefficient $. Left: near $J=1$, $h(J)$ and $-r\log J$ alone are visually indistinguishable, and both diverge as $J\to 0^+$. Right: on a log scale, $-r\log J$ alone decreases without bound, and $h(J)$ tracks it closely until the quadratic term alone finally overtakes it near $J^\ast \approx 9550$, the point where $h(J)$ starts to grow. This $J^\ast $ is far beyond any dilation this RVE's data ever reaches; the total trained energy nonetheless grows steeply for realistic stretches, driven by the sixth-power terms of Proposition~\ref {prop:sixth-power-bound} below rather than by $h(J)$ itself (Figure~\ref {fig:volumetric})}{figure.9}{}}
